ription section\n4. Use `<details>` and `<summary>` elements for collapsible sections:\n   - `<details open>` for History (default expanded)\n   - `<details>` for Plan, Questions (conditional), Available Actions\n   - Empty sections still render as `<details>` (collapsed)\n5. Style with CSS for consistent look\n6. Add `aria-expanded` attributes for accessibility\n\n### Naming Conventions\nUse exact field names from code:\n- `impl_spec` (not \"Implementation Spec\")\n- `test_spec` (not \"Test Spec\")\n- `impl_notes` (not \"Implementation Notes\")\n- `plan`\n- `history`\n- `description`\n\n### Accessibility Considerations\n- TUI: Textual's Collapsible provides keyboard support (Enter/Space to toggle)\n- Web UI: Use `<details>`/`<summary>` which have native accessibility, add `aria-expanded`\n- Focus management when toggling sections\n\n### Edge Cases\n- Very long content: Use `max-height` with `overflow-y: auto` in web UI; use `VerticalScroll` in TUI\n- Empty sections: Render collapsed `<details>` or `Collapsible` but do not hide entirely\n- Questions form in web UI: Conditionally wrap in collapsible based on stage !== 'requested-input'"
